tatistics and school direct., 1969-71 (Ministry of Education and Community Development)03594cz  a2200361n  n  78002277 DLC20180821073824.0780119n| azannaabn          |n aaa        an  78002277   a(OCoLC)oca00138902  aDLCbengerdacDLCdDLCdOCoLCdNNYU-HJdDLCdIdBB  f1947-11-062edtf1 aAiello, Barbara  aCrypto-Jews  aPittsburgh (Pa.)cItalyeMilan (Italy)eCalabria (Italy)fSarasota (Fla.)2naf  eSerrastretta (Italy)  mwww.rabbibarbara.com  aJudaism--Study and teachingaCrypto-Jews--ItalyaJewish outreach2lcsh  aIndiana University of PennsylvaniaaGeorge Washington University2naf  aRabbinical Seminary InternationalaRabbinical Academy (New York. N.Y.)aItalian Jewish Cultural Center of CalabriaaB'nei AnusimaRadio Rabbi (Radio program)  aSinagoga Ner Tamid del Suds2006  aRabbis2lcsh  aFemales2lcdgt  aengaita  aPlaces and spaces, 1976 (a.e.)bt.p. (Barbara Aiello)  aHer Business is looking up, 1988:bCIP t.p. (Barbara Aiello) data sheet (b. 11-6-47) pub. info. (pres. and founder, The Kids on the Block)  aAiello, Barbara. The Cat that ate the cannoli, 2015:btitle page (Rabbi Barbara Aiello) page 71 (Rabbi Barbara Aiello is the first woman rabbi and first non-orthodox rabbi in Italy. Following her rabbinate in Italy's first modern liberal synagogue in Milan, she returned to her ancestral home in Calabria to found Sinagoga Ner Tamid del Sud, in Serrastretta in 2006. She is also founder of the B'nei Anusim movement of southern Italy. She directs the Italian Jewish Cultural Center of Calabria and is host of the Radio Rabbi program, a Jewish radio broadcast on WLSS AM 930 in Sarasota, Florida. Her website is: www.rabbibarbara.com.)  aWikipedia, viewed April 30, 2018bBarbara Aiello (She was born in Pittsburgh to a family of Italian Jewish origin and was ordained at the Rabbinical Seminary International in New York at the age of 51. In 2005 she conducted the first Passover Seder in Sicily since 1492, when the Jews were expelled. She also founded the Italian Jewish Cultural Center of Calabria and Sinagoga Ner Tamid del Sud, the first active synagogue in 500 years in Calabria.)uhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbara_Aiello  aRabbi Barbara Aiello website, viewed April 30, 2018bBarbara Aiello (She holds a MS from The George Washington University in Washington DC and received "smeicha" (rabbinic ordination) from The Rabbinical Seminary International and the Rabbinical Academy in New York City. Rabbi Barbara Aiello's mission starts in southern Italy where she works to help "anousim" (Italians whose ancestors were forced into conversion from Judaism) discover and connect with their Jewish roots.)uhttps://rabbibarbara.com/about/rabbi_barbara_aiello/  aGoogle.com, viewed April 30, 2018bBarbara Aiello (Born November 6, 1947 (age 70 years), Pittsburgh)uhttps://www.google.com/search?q=rabbi+barbara+aiello&rls=com.microsoft:en-US:IE-Address&ie=UTF-8&oe=UTF-8&sourceid=ie7&rlz=1I7RNRB_enUS554&gws_rd=ssl  aTrick or treat or trouble, c1989:btitle page (Barbara Aiello) page 55 (The Kids on the Block puppet program was founded in 1977 by Barbara Aiello)  aEmail from Barbara Aiello, 18 August 2018:b(She is the author of "Places and Spaces" and is the creator and founder of "The Kids on the Block." She has been an ordained rabbi since 1999)00772cz  a2200193n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040004100115100001200156374003200168400002000200670004700220670002700267670009300294670019100387n  78002846 DLC20180822073600.0780126n| azannaabn          |a aaa        an  78002846   a(OCoLC)oca00139460  aDLCbengerdacDLCdUkOxUdDLCdMiEM0 aBeshlie  aArtistsaIllustrators2lcsh1 aNewman, Beshlie  aHer Snailsleap Lane, 1977:bt.p. (Beshlie)  aGB 77-32258b(Beshlie)  aThe mouse house, 2005:bt.p. (Beshlie Newman) cover, etc. (illustrations signed Beshlie)  aWayfarers all, 2015:btitle page (Beshlie) page 4 of cover (Beshlie; arti