 aaa        an  85062755   aDLCbengerdacDLC  f19472edtf1 aRamos, María Elena,d1947-  aHavana (Cuba)2naf  fCaracas (Venezuela)2naf  aPhilosophy2lcsh  aGalería de Arte Nacional (Venezuela)2nafs1976  aUniversidad Católica Andrés Bello2naf  aCentro de Enseñanza Gráfica  aUniversidad Simon Bolívar2naf  aMuseo de Bellas Artes (Venezuela)2nafs1989t2001  aMuseo de Arte Popular de Petare Bárbaro Rivas2naf  aInstituto de Educación Superior Armando Reverón  aProfessoraArt criticaCuratoraSocial communicator  aFemales2lcdgt  aspa  aHer Un museo para la paz, 1984:bt.p. (María Elena Ramos) verso t.p., etc. (b. La Habana, 1947; has lived in Venezuela since 1950; professor, Centro de Enseñanza Gráfica; lists works; published by the Departamento de Relaciones Públicas de Lagoven in Caracas)  aColección Cisneros website, August 23, 2018:b(María Elena Ramos; degree in social communication from the Universidad Católica Andrés Bello; master's and PhD in philosophy from the Universidad Simon Bolívar; she was president of the Museo de Bellas Artes in Caracas (1989-2001); founding member of the Galería de Arte Nacional (Venezuela) (1976), and the Museo de Arte Popular de Petare; member of the team that created the Instituto de Educación Superior Armando Reverón in the 1980s; since 1976 she has been a lecturer at universities and museums in Venezuela, Latin America, United States, Spain, and France; author of El Ávila en la mirada de todos, 2014; La cultura bajo acoso, 2012; Gego, 2012; Diálogos con el arte, 2007; Fotociudad. Estética urbana y lenguaje fotográfico, 2003; De las formas del arte, 2002; Armónico-Disonante, 2001;  Acciones frente a la plaza, 1995; Diálogo con lo natural, 1992; Pistas para quedar mirando, Academia Nacional de la Historia, 1991, and Arte y naturaleza, 1987; some of her curatorial projects are Ética-Estética Política, 2013; Contaminados, 2012; Pasión y razón de un espíritu constructivo (Torres-García y la Escuela del Sur), Biarritz, 2006; Árboles, Bienal Internacional del Barro, Caracas, 2001; Christian Boltanski: Sombras, Caracas, l999; Intervenciones en el espacio (artists: Kosuth, Graham, Camnitzer, Caramelle y otros), 1995; Jesús Soto : La Física, lo Inmaterial, Museo de Arte Moderno Jesús Soto, 1993; and Alejandro Otero : Las Estructuras de la Realidad, Bienal Internacional de Sao Paulo, 1991; she has been the curator for Venezuela in several international biennials: Venice, São Paulo, Medellín, and Cuenca)uhttp://www.coleccioncisneros.org/authors/mar%C3%ADa-elena-ramos  aInternational Center for the Arts of the Americas website, August 23, 2018:b(María Elena Ramos; born 1947; formerly affiliated with the Centro de Enseñanza Gráfica; Venezuelan curator; author of several works including Alejandro Otero : Las Estructuras de la Realidad, Bienal Internacional de Sao Paulo, 1991)uhttp://icaadocs.mfah.org/icaadocs/THEARCHIVE/FullRecord/tabid/88/doc/1154316/language/en-US/Default.aspxuhttp://icaadocs.mfah.org/icaadocs/THEARCHIVE/Browse/Authors/tabid/84/k/A/e/1220851/page/1/language/en-US/Default.aspx01052cz  a2200277n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040004400115046001500159053001600174100003300190370001500223373003000238400004200268400003200310400004100342400003100383400004200414670008000456670009000536670010500626670004300731n  85065054 DLC20180824135455.0850920n| azannaabn          |a aaa        an  85065054   a(OCoLC)oca01432113  aDLCbengerdacDLCdDLCdOCoLCdUkdDLC  f14362edtf 0aPK2579.T6961 aTripathy, Biyot Kesh,d1936-  aIndia2naf  aBerhampur University2naf1 aTripathy, B. K.q(Biyot Kesh),d1936-0 aBiyot Kesh Tripathy,d1936-0 aBiẏatkeśa Tripāṭhī,d1936-0 aBiyotkesh Tripathy,d1936-1 aTripāṭhī, Biẏatkeśa,d1936-  aAuthor's Osiris N., 1985:bt.p. (Biyot Kesh Tripathy; Berhampur University)  aLC data base, 9/18/85b(hd