smāʻīl,d-1371.tKitāb ṣafwat al-ṣafā0 aTawakkul ibn Ismāʻīl,d-1371.tMawāhib al-sanīyah fī al-manāqib al-ṣafawīyah0 aTawakkul ibn Ismāʻīl,d-1371.tṢafwat aṣ-ṣafā0 aTawakkul ibn Ismāʻīl,d-1371.tṢifwat al-ṣafā0 aTawakkul ibn Ismāʻīl,d-1371.tṢafvatuʾṣ-ṣafā0 wnneaaTawakkul ibn Ismāʻīl,dd. 1371.tṢafwat al-ṣafā  aZirke, H. Ein hagiographisches Zeugnis zur persischen Geschichte ... 1987:bt.p. (das achte Kapitel des Ṣafwat aṣ-ṣafā) p. 1-2 (life of Sheik Ṣafī ad-Dīn from Ardabīl, a mystic and head of a religious order; b.d. unknown; d. 1334; written about 20 yrs. after Safī's death by the scribe Tawakkulī b. Ismaʻīl b. Ḥāǧǧī al-Ardabīlī called Ibn-i Bazzāz; d.d. given as 1371; title: Kitāb al-Mawāhib as-saniyya fīl-manāqib as-ṣafawiyya, or for short: Ṣafwat aṣ-ṣafā, the latter being the predominant usage) added t.p. (Kitāb Ṣafwat al-ṣafā; al-Mawāhib al-sanīyah fī al-manāqib al-ṣafawīyah)  aEIb(under: Tawakkul b. Bazzaz; Ṣifwat al-Ṣafā, life of Shaikh Ṣafī al-Dīn al-Ardabīlī authored by Tawakkul b. Bazzāz; work consists of app. 216,000 words)  aRypka. History of Iranian literatureb(under: Ibn-i Bazzāz; life of Shaykh Ṣafī, ancestor of the Safavids ... his sayings and miracles, form the theme of the Ṣafvatuʾṣ-ṣafāʾ, "The purest of the pure" by Tavakkulī b. Ismāʻīl al-Ardabīlī; written twenty-four years after Shaykh Ṣafī's death)  aBM. Cat. of Persian mss.:bAdd. 11745 (under: Ṣafwat al-Ṣafā; an account of the life and miracles of the celebrated saint, Shaikh Ṣafī ud-Dīn Isḥāḳ b. Shaikh Amīn ud-Dīn Jabrāʾīl ul-Musavi, ancestor of the Safavids; contains a preface, introd., twelve sections (bāb), and an appendix (khātimah); authored by Tavakkulī; also known as: Darvīsh Tavakkul b. Ismāʻīl; commonly known as Ibn Bazzāz)02824cz  a2200385n  n  88032852 DLC20180824073300.0890106n| azannaabn          |a aaa        an  88032852   a(OCoLC)oca02434957  aDLCbengerdacDLCdDLCdCaAEUdWaUdScU  f1951-10-152edtf1 aDevor, Aaron H.,d1951-  cVictoria (B.C.)2naf  mahdevor@uvic.ca  aGender nonconformityaTransgender people--Sexual behavioraSociology2lcsh  aUniversity of Victoria (B.C.)2naf  aTransgender Archives2naf  aUniversity of Washingtont1990  aSimon Fraser Universityt1985  aYork University (Toronto, Ont.)t1971  aCollege teachersaSociologistsaSexologists2lcsh  aFemales2lcdgts1951t2002  aMales2lcdgts2002  aeng1 wnneaDevor, Holly  aGender blending, c1989:btitle page (Holly Devor)  aFTM: female-to-male transsexuals in society, 1997:bCIP t.p. (Holly Devor) data sheet (b. Oct. 15, 1951)  aDevor, Aaron H. The Transgender Archives, 2014:btitle page (Aaron H. Devor)  aWikipedia, viewed 28 April 2016:bAaron Devor (Aaron H. Devor; born in 1951; a Canadian sociologist and sexologist known for research of transsexuality and transgender communities; he has taught at the University of Victoria since 1989 and is currently dean of graduate studies; earned a bachelor's degree in psychology from York University in 1971, a master's degree in communications from Simon Fraser University in 1985, and a Ph.D. in sociology from the University of Washington in 1990; a trans man, Devor transitioned in 2002 at age 51)  aAaron H Devor web site, viewed 28 April 2016b(professor of sociology, former Dean of Graduate Studies, and the Founder and Academic Director of the Transgender Archives at the University of Victoria, Canada; specializes in the study of gender, sex, and sexuality in transgender people)  aAmicus database, 28 April 2016b(authorized access points: Devor, Aaron H., 1951- (Canadian, born 1951-10-15) and Devor, Holly (variant, Devor, Holly Joy))  aOut of the closet, into the archives, 2015:bpage 338 (Aaron H. Devor, PhD has been studying and teaching about transgender-related questions for thirty years. Dr. Devor is the founder and academic 