ph Pénicaud; André Joseph Pénigault; André Joseph Pérricault; born in La Rochelle, France, around 1680; carpenter and chronicler; claimed to have accompanied Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville on his first voyage to Louisiana in 1698; on Sept. 24, 1699, Pénicaut signed a deed of indenture as a ship's carpenter; went on Iberville's second voyage to Louisiana aboard Le Marin and established himself in Mobile; later said that in 1701 he accompanied Pierre Charles Le Sueur on an expedition to the upper Mississippi to copper mines in what is now Minnesota; also stated that he accompanied Iberville on the lower Mississippi; these expeditions, however, occurred simultaneously; claimed to have been with Louis Juchereau de St. Denis on his trip across Texas to San Juan Bautista to open trade with the Spaniards around 1714; a master carpenter when he left Mobile to return to France in October 1721; after his return he wrote his Annals, an account of St. Denis's journey that has been labeled both fact and fiction;one author states, probably wrongly, that he returned to Louisiana and was the man named Pérricault, a carpenter, who escaped the Nachez Massacre in 1729 and took the news to New Orleans; scholars do credit Pénicaut with his fairly accurate descriptions of the lower Mississippi River and surrounding regions)01291cz  a2200253n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040003500115100003300150370003700183372006500220373008500285375001700370377000800387400005100395400002600446400003300472670010300505670010400608670032500712n  88079957 DLC20180822073537.0880304n| azannaabn          |a aaa        an  88079957   a(OCoLC)oca02218496  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCoLCdIEN1 aCarvalho, Carlos A. da Costa  fMozambiquefRwandafBelgium2naf  aDemographyaMozambique--PopulationaRwanda--Population2lcsh  aUniversité catholique de Louvain (1970- ). Département de démographie2naf  aMales2lcdgt  afre1 aCarvalho, C. A. da Co