 Philipp,d1960-  cU.S.fSoutheast Asia  aSecurity, InternationalaPhilosophy2lcsh  aGeneva Centre for the Democratic Control of Armed ForcesaUniversität BernaUniversité de Fribourg. Ost-Europa InstitutaPécsi TudományegyetemaLuhansʹkyĭ nat︠s︡ionalʹnyĭ pedahohichnyĭ universytet imeni Tarasa Shevchenka2naf  aSpecialistsaCollege teachers2lcsh1 aFluri, F.,d1960-1 aFluri, Ph.q(Philipp),d1960-1 aFluri, Philipp H.,d1960-1 aFurūri, Firippu,d1960-1 aFluri, Philippe,d1960-  aEinsicht in Insight, c1988:bt.p. (Philipp Fluri) p. 182 (Philipp H. Fluri; Dr. phil. hist.; b. 5-5-1960 in Balsthal, Switzerland)  aPravovye akty Rossiĭskoĭ Federat︠s︡ii v sfere voenno-grazhdanskikh otnosheniĭ, 2004:bt.p. verso (F. Fluri; Ph. Fluri)  aGikai ni yoru anzen hoshō bumon no kanshi, 2008:bt.p. (Firippu Furūri [in kana])  aDie traditionelle chinesische Wissenschaft, 1993:btitle page (Philippe Fluri) page preceding title page (Philipp Fluri)  aDCAF WWW site, July 24, 2013:bStaff (Deputy Director of the Geneva Centre for the Democratic Control of Armed Forces (DCAF); international security expert; studied philosophy and social sciences; doctoral degrees from the Universities of Bern and Fribourg; graduate of the East European Studies Institute at Fribourg University; has performed extensive post-doctoral research in South East Asia and the US; Visiting Professor at the University of Pecs, Hungary; Honorary Professor of Taras Shevchenko Pedagogical University, Ukraine)01626cz  a2200325n  n  90609493 DLC20180825073426.0900208n| azannaabn          |b aaa        an  90609493   a(OCoLC)oca02683421  aDLCbengerdacDLCdDLCdOCoLCdDNGAdDLCdInU  f1898-07-30g1944-10-092edtf1 aDicker, Friedl,d1898-1944  aVienna (Austria)bBrzezinka (Województwo Małopolskie, Poland)2naf  aArtistsaEducators2lcsh  aFemales2lcdgt1 aDicker-Brandeis, Friedl,d1898-19441 aBrandeis, Friedl Dicker-,d1898-19441 aDicker, Friedericke,d