 of Hartford Connecticut and Boston Massachusetts included Sam Reed (vocals), Steve Starger (keyboards), Peter Zummo (trombone), Bob Carabillo (sax), Rick Albani (trumpet), Shelly Rosen (bass), Ronnie Deutch (drums) and Barry Grant (guitar). Most of the original material on the album was written by Steve Starger. Most of the original material on the album was written by Steve Starger and the album was produced by Jim Mason (Poco, The Fabulous Rhinestones) and engineered by Jack Sherdel. Felix Pappalardi (Cream, Mountain) was among the guest artists and played flute and strings on several tracks. A later edition of the group changed personnel with bassists David Wofford and Wolf Gianandes, vocalist Blandy Ingraham and drummer Chuck Wansley)01166cz  a2200241n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040003600115046000900151100002100160370006900181372010400250374004600354375001100400377000800411670005900419670021900478670012100697670010600818n  92106022 DLC20180822073625.0921029n| azannaabn          |n aaa        an  92106022   a(OCoLC)oca03263704  aDLCbengerdacDLCdIlMpPLdIEN  f19591 aOnyefulu, Ifeoma  aOnitsha (Nigeria)cNigeriacGreat BritaineLondon (England)2naf  aChildren's literatureaIllustrated children's booksaChildren's stories, EnglishaPhotography2lcsh  aAuthorsaPhotographersaJournalists2lcsh  afemale  aeng  aHer A is for Africa, 1993:bCIP t.p. (Ifeoma Onyefulu)  aClothes, 2012:bjacket flap (Ifeoma Onyefulu was brought up in a traditional village in Eastern Nigeria; her highly acclaimed children's books are renowned for countering negative images of Africa; lives in London)  aIfeoma Onyefulu website, viewed Nov. 17, 2014:bbanner (Ifeoma Onyefulu; writer, children's author and photographer)  aWikipedia, August 21, 2018b(Ifeoma Onyefulu; born 1959 in Onitsha, Anambra, Nigeria; Igbo ethnicity)00911cz  a2200253n  450000100130000000300040001300500170001700800410003401000170007