(Henry Toledano) p. [3] (born in Egypt; sent to a public school in England; degree in economics from London University; has been part owner of two book stores and presently sells out of print books online)  aHis website, viewed 22 Aug. 2018b(Henry Toledano was born and raised in Egypt. At the age of fourteen, he was sent to a public school in England. He then went to universities in London and New York. Subsequently, he traveled around the world for two years while doing various jobs. He moved to the Bahamas in the mid-1960s and became associate editor for the local paper in Nassau. Ten years later, he relocated to San Francisco and, for the last thirty-five years, has been in the retail book business - first, as a partner in a new bookstore, and then, for a longer period, in a used one. Lists his books)01617cz  a2200229n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002800115046002100143100001900164370003100183373006100214374006700275375001700342377000800359670010600367670061500473670029901088n  96061564 DLC20180821073930.0960621n| azannaabn          |n aaa        an  96061564   a(OCoLC)oca04104925  aDLCbengerdacDLCdICU  f1949-03-122edtf1 aPopelka, Pavel  aStrání (Czech Repubic)  aMuzeum Jana Amose Komenského v Uherském Brodě2naf  aEthnologistsaFolkloristsaJournalistsaMuseum directors2lcsh  aMales2lcdgt  acze  aPříběhy v písních vyzpívané, 1995:bt.p. (Pavel Popelka) colophon (PhDr. Pavel Popelka)  aDatabazeKnih.cz WWW site, August 20, 2018:bPavel Popelka page, Životopis tab (Pavel Popelka; born 1949; ethnographer and journalist; director of the Muzeum Jana Amose Komenského v Uherském Brodě; member of the program board of the international folklore festival in Strážnice and founder and organizer of the Festival of Lenten Traditions [Festival masopustních tradic] in Strání; collaborator for culture and social activity for ZVUK in the Zlínský kraj and regular contrib