a is Senior Research Fellow and Head of Justice and Home Affairs Programme at CEPS. He is also Part-Time Professor at the Migration Policy Centre (MPC) in the European University Institute (EUI) in Florence (Italy).    Carrera is Visiting Professor at the Paris School of International Affairs (PSIA) at Sciences Po (France), Associate Professor/Senior Research Fellow at the Faculty of Law in Maastricht University (The Netherlands), and Honorary Industry Professor at the School of Law in Queen Mary University of London (UK).     His main research interests are on EU justice and home affairs (JHA) law and Area of Freedom, Security and Justice policy, with particular focus on migration, asylum, citizenship and Schengen policies").  aPolicing humanitarianism, 2019:bECIP data view ("Sergio Carrera is Senior Research Fellow and Head of Justice and Home Affairs Programme at CEPS and Professor at the Migration Policy Centre (MPC) in the European University Institute in Florence"),00787cz  a2200169n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010004500075040002800120100007800148400005900226400008800285670003400373670009800407670011200505n 2006037048DLC20180824135413.0060510n| azannaabn          |a aaa        an 2006037048zno 98009896 zn 2008070108  aDLCbengerdacDLCdDLC1 aHérold, Ferdinand,d1791-1833.tPré aux clercs.pJours de mon enfance1 aHérold, Ferdinand,d1791-1833.tJours de mon enfance1 aHérold, Ferdinand,d1791-1833.tAria de l'opéra Le pré aux cleres de Hérold  aAir chanté par Mme. Casimir  aFrench coloratura arias, 2004, p1994:bcontainer (Jours de mon enfance (Le pré aux clercs))  aLe pré aux clercs. No. 4, Air chanté par Mme. Casimir, 1835?:bp. 1 (first words: Jours de mon enfance)00721cz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040003600115046002100151100002900172670010000201670026200301n 2006038804DLC20180822073428.0060516n| azannaabn          |n aaa       