d by Robert M. Cooper)  aInternet Broadway database, March 5, 2009b(Robert M. Cooper; Male; Director, Producer)  aChicago tribune WWW site, viewed Aug. 14, 2018b(in obituary dated Aug. 6, 2018: Robert Miller Cooper studied and acted at Chicago's Goodman School of Drama and later worked in Chicago's industrial film industry before beginning a career as a Tony Award-nominated producer and director of musicals both on and off-Broadway in New York City; Cooper, 86, died July 14 in New York City; had been a New York City resident for the past 50 years; born and raised in Detroit; moved to Chicago; worked as a freelance actor and writer in Chicago before joining Take Ten Inc., a Chicago film producer, where he served as artistic director; Take Ten developed original musicals, industrial shows, movies, and radio and TV commercials; in 1968, Cooper moved to New York City, where he continued to work remotely for Take Ten; soon began working as a producer and director for several companies, including Comart Aniforms, where he worked to produce and stage a 40-hour educational TV series, "The Place of Doors," as well as several industrial and theme park shows; returned to theater by the 1970s; one of the highlights of Cooper's career was directing and producing "Bubbling Brown Sugar," a musical revue)00514cz  a2200145n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040002800092046001500120100002100135670006400156670014800220n 2009015397DLC20180823124924.0090312n| azannaabn          |n aaa        an 2009015397  aDLCbengerdacDLCdDLC  f19782edtf1 aPascaru, Mariana  aAndreescu, Florin. România, 2008:bt.p. (Mariana Pascaru)  aBiblioteca Centrală Universitară "Lucian Blaga" Cluj-Napoca online authority file, Aug. 23, 2018:b(hdg.: Pascaru, Mariana Dorina (1978- ))00399cz  a2200145n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002400115053001800139100002100157670007500178n 2009015484DLC201808220