74 and left the police force the next year. She spent the next 15 years as a prosecutor in the U.S. attorney's office for the District of Columbia, until her appointment as a Superior Court judge in 1990. She presided over family, civil and criminal trials, taking senior status for 12 years in 2003 to work part time. She was a colored-pencil artist and a docent at the Supreme Court, where she gave lectures and conducted tours)00802cz  a2200229n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040003700115046002100152110004500173368003700218370002400255372002000279377000800299410005100307670006300358670007300421670007800494no 91003397 DLC20180822073403.0910207n| azannaabn          |a ana     c  ano 91003397   a(OCoLC)oca02892481  aMoSU-LbengerdacMoSU-LdMoSU-L  s1861t18622edtf1 aNorth Carolina.bConventiond(1861-1862)  aCongresses and conventions2lcsh  fNorth Carolina2naf  aSecession2lcsh  aeng1 aNorth Carolina.bState Conventiond(1861-1862)  aMcCormick, J.G. Personnel of the Convention of 1861, 1900.  aOCLC database, 2-7-91b(hdg.: North Carolina. Convention, 1861-1862)  aOrdinances passed by the State Convention at its adjourned session, 1861.00836cz  a2200229n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002800115046003300143100002300176368002100199370004500220374001800265375001700283377000800300378002100308670006900329670020800398no 91003531 DLC20180823073253.0910208n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano 91003531   a(OCoLC)oca02895070  aCLUbengerdacCLUdUPB  f1912-12-09g1986-03-262edtf1 aRobinson, Bartlett  cAmericans2lcdgt  aNew York (N.Y.)bFallbrook (Calif.)2naf  aActors2lcdgt  aMales2lcdgt  aeng  qBartlett Whitney  aPlayhouse 90. The tunnel [MP] 1959:bcredits (Bartlett Robinson)  aIMDB, 22 August 2018b(Bartlett Robinson; birth name: Bartlett Whitney Robinson; actor; born December 9, 1912 in New York City, New Yor