 University of California at Berkeley in 1957 and received a doctorate in political science from Harvard University in 1961. Dr. Lyman was the State Department's director of refugee affairs from 1989 to 1992. After returning from South Africa, he was a State Department liaison to the United Nations. After retiring in 1999, he held posts at the Aspen Institute, U.S. Institute for Peace and Council on Foreign Relations. From 2011 to 2013, he served as the special envoy to Sudan)00499cz  a2200169n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002800115100001800143374002200161377000800183670005500191670008300246no 95052871 DLC20180824073347.0951107n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano 95052871   a(OCoLC)oca03954307  aTNJbengerdacTNJdNjP1 aPitta, Helena  aTranslators2lcsh  apor  aArt da prudencia, 1994:bverso t.p. (Helena Pitta)  aPTBNP in VIAF, June 5, 2018b(Pitta, Helena; graduated in History; translator)00986cz  a2200241n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040004600115046003300161100002900194368002100223370005100244372003200295374002000327375001700347378001700364670006900381670004700450670024700497no 95057979 DLC20180823073339.0951208n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano 95057979   a(OCoLC)oca03970973  aCLUbengerdacCLUdCLU-FTdCStdIENdUPB  f1919-07-19g2010-03-112edtf1 aDunlap, Paul,d1919-2010  cAmericans2lcdgt  aSpringfield (Ohio)bPalm Springs (Calif.)2naf  aMotion picture music2lcgft  aComposers2lcsh  aMales2lcdgt  qPaul William  aFrontier gun [MP] 1958:bcredits (music composed by Paul Dunlap)  aOCLC, 11-6-95b(hdg.: Dunlap, Paul, 1919-)  aInternet movie database WWW site, April 6, 2010; 22 August 2018b(Paul Dunlap; b. July 19, 1919, Springfield, Ohio; birth name, Paul William Dunlap; d. March 11, 2010 in Palm Springs, California; film composer; alternate name, Paul A. Dunlap)01153cz  a2200229n  450000100130