hn Porcellino) jacket (b. in Chicago in 1968)  aWikipedia, August 10, 2018b(John Porcellino; born September 18, 1968, in Chicago, Illinois; grew up in Hoffman Estates, Illinois; creator of minicomics; has suffered from major depression since he was a teenager; lived in Denver, Colorado, from 1992-1998; suffered from hyperacusis; had removal of a benign tumor from his small intestine  aKing-Cat comics by John Porcellino website, August 10, 2018:bHistory (John Porcellino was born in Chicago, in 1968, and has been writing, drawing, and publishing minicomics, comics, and graphic novels for over thirty years. His celebrated self-published series King-Cat Comics, begun in 1989, has inspired a generation of cartoonists. Diary of a Mosquito Abatement Man, a collection of King-Cat stories about Porcellino's experiences as a pest control worker, won an Ignatz Award in 2005, and Perfect Example, first published in 2000, chronicles his struggles with depression as a teenager. King-Cat Classix and Map of My Heart, published in 2007/2009, offer a comprehensive overview of the zine's first sixty-one issues, while Thoreau at Walden (2008) is a poetic expression of the great philosopher's experience and ideals; currently lives in Beloit, Wisconsin)uhttp://www.king-cat.net/history/01219cz  a2200205n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040003800115046002100153100003000174370002500204378001500229400003500244670016300279670019900442670037200641no2003021700DLC20180822073640.0030306n| azannaabn          |a aaa        ano2003021700  a(OCoLC)oca05989883  aDLC-SbengerdacDLC-SdDLCdDNLM  f1944-12-232edtf1 aNichols, David E.,d1944-  aCovington (Ky.)2naf  qDavid Earl1 wnneaNichols, David E.,cPh.D.  aThe Heffter review of psychedelic research, 1998:bt.p. (David E. Nichols, Ph.D.) p. 2 of cover (School of Pharmacy and Pharmacal Sciences, Purdue University)  aBehavioral neurobiology of psychedelic drugs, 2018:bt.p