     c  ano2006102169  a(OCoLC)oca07062274  aMH-HYbengcMH-HYdOCoLCdDLC1 aKang, Yong-nam1 a강 룡남1 a강 영남  aTHIS 1XX FIELD CANNOT BE USED UNDER RDA UNTIL THIS UNDIFFERENTIATED RECORD HAS BEEN HANDLED FOLLOWING THE GUIDELINES IN DCM Z1 008/32  aMachine-derived non-Latin script reference project.  aNon-Latin script reference not evaluated.  a[Author of Chosŏn kodaesa yŏn'gu]  aChosŏn kodaesa yŏn'gu, 2004:bv. 2, colophon  (강 룡남 = Kang Yong-nam; res. of North Korea)  a[Added entry of Chuyoguk ŭi oeja tojip chedo]  aChuyoguk ŭi oeja tojip chedo, 1970:bt.p. (강 영남 = Kang Yŏng-nam)03059cz  a2200361n  no2006102188DLC20180823073259.0060926n| azannaabn          |a aaa     c  ano20061021887 aB0004162bdusc7 ahttp://bioguide.congress.gov/scripts/biodisplay.pl?index=B0004162uri7 a69168352findagr7 ahttp://www.findagrave.com/memorial/69168352uri7 a785408252viaf7 ahttp://viaf.org/viaf/785408252uri7 aQ13324622wikidata7 ahttp://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13324622uri  a(OCoLC)oca07062293  aSdMadTbengerdacSdMadTdSd  f1902-10-06g1999-04-012edtf1 aBerry, Ellis Yarnal,d1902-1999  aLarchwood (Iowa)bRapid City (S.D.)eWashington (D.C.)eKennebec (S.D.)eMcLaughlin (S.D.)eRapid City (S.D.)fPhilip (S.D.)fCorson County (S.D.)2naf  aMorningside College (Sioux City, Iowa)aUniversity of South DakotaaUniversity of South Dakota. School of Law2naf  aSouth Dakota. Legislature. Senate2nafs1939t1942  aUnited States. Congress. House2nafs1951-01-03t1971-01-03  aLawyersaLegislatorsaRepublican Party members (United States)2lcdgt  aPublishers2itoamc  aMales2lcdgt  aeng1 aBerry, E. Y.,d1902-1999  aSouth Dakota legislature legislator historical listing WWW site, Sept. 26, 2006b(Ellis Yarnal "E.Y." Berry; b. Oct. 6, 1902; d. Apr. 1, 1999; Republican state senator, 1939-1942; Republican U.S. Representative, 1951-1971)  aWikipedia, August 22, 2018b(Ellis Yarnall Berry (October 6, 1902 - April 1, 1999) was an attorney, newspaper publisher and politician, elected to the United States House of Representatives. Berry was born in Larchwood, Iowa, and graduated from Philip High School in Philip, South Dakota. He was a student at Morningside College from 1920 through 1922. He transferred to the University of South Dakota, where he completed his undergraduate work and studied law, graduating with a law degree in 1927. He was admitted to the bar that same year under diploma privilege. Berry started his law practice in Kennebec, South Dakota; two years later, he moved to McLaughlin. He was elected as state's attorney, probate court judge for Corson County, and mayor of McLaughlin. He served as the publisher of the newspaper Mclaughlin Messenger beginning in 1938. He was editor of the State Bar Association Journal from 1938 through 1950. Berry was elected to the South Dakota State Senate from 1938 through 1942, a total of two terms. In 1950, Berry was elected as a Republican to the United States House of Representatives, and reelected nine consecutive times, retiring in 1971. Beginning in 1952, he also published the McIntosh News and Morristown World. After retiring from Congress, Berry he settled in Rapid City, South Dakota. He lived there until his death in 1999)uhttp://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellis_Yarnal_Berry00399cz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002800115100002600143375001900169377000800188670004500196no2006103232DLC20180822073535.0060928n| azannaabn           n aaa     c  ano2006103232  a(OCoLC)oca07064958  aRPBbengerdacRPBdNcU1 aSharpe, Stella Gentry  aFemales2lcdgt  aeng  aTobe, 1939:bt.p. (Stella Gentry Sharpe)00934cz  a2200217n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002700115046003300142100002700175370004200202372002200244374002400266375001700290378002400307670009900331670028600430no2006106481DLC20180822073536.0060809n| azann