t. p. (D.L. Henderson)  aGoogle search, August 15, 2018b(Dr. D L Henderson is a cemetery historian, genealogist, and preservationist whose research and writing focuses on the intersection of history, memory, and culture in African American life. She is a member of the Historic Oakland Foundation Board of Directors, the Historic South-View Foundation Board of Advisors, and the Historic Rural Churches of Georgia Advisory Board. She has been awarded the Atlanta Urban Design Commission's Jenny D. Thurston Memorial Award to an Outstanding Preservation Professional, and she has been recognized by the Atlanta City Council for her contribution to the preservation and interpretation of African American history and culture. She researches, lectures, and conducts tours on cemetery history and the art and architecture of South-View and Oakland cemeteries, two cities of the dead in Atlanta, Georgia)uhttps://www.amazon.com/D-L-Henderson/e/B07C71FPPF/ref=dbs_p_pbk_rwt_abau00854nz  a2200229n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002900115046000700144100002100151370006300172372002300235373003700258374002100295375001600316377000800332670014400340670014000484no2018110302DLC20180822073024.0180817n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano2018110302  a(OCoLC)oca11504733  aWlAbNLbengerdacWlAbNL  s201 aUmbanhowar, John  cUnited StateseMinnesotaeIdahoeLos Angeles (Calif.)2naf  aArchitecture2lcsh  aHughesumbanhowar Architects2naf  aArchitects2lcsh  aMales2lcsh  aeng  aHughesumbanhowar Architects : The Architecture of Scott Hughes and John Umbanhowar:bt.p. (John Umbanhowar ; co-founder of HUUM architects)  aVoyage LA WWW site, viewed 15 August 2018b(John Umbanhowar was raised in Minnesota and Idaho ; lives in Los Angeles ; [image of male])00960nz  a2200241n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002900115046002100144100002300165370004100188372004100229373002700270