dea of a bureaucratic career and began his artistic training with Charlet and, later, Paul Delaroche. His first albums of sketches were published in 1839. The pseudonym Cham refers both to his initials (Charles Henri Amédée), and to his status as the son of the French count Noé (Noé is the French name for the Biblical Noah, whose son Ham is known in French as Cham). He became a prolific cartoonist, whose distinctive style (based on a select cast of grotesque, grimacing 'puppets' and amusing captions summing up the news of the day) brought him great success throughout his life. Satirical, humorous renderings of works exhibited at the official Salons were another favorite theme. Sadly, his work has not aged well.uhttp://www.delart.org/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/Cham-Amedee-Charles-Henri.pdf00958nz  a2200217n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002900115100003800144370001500182372005100197373003700248374003300285375001100318377000800329400003800337670036500375no2018110340DLC20180822073033.0180817n| azannaabn          |a aaa     c  ano2018110340  a(OCoLC)oca11504771  aCL-CcUbengcCL-CcUerda1 aSanhueza Retamal, Claudia Eugenia  cChile2naf  aAgricultural engineeringaFarm equipment2lcsh  aUniversidad de Concepción2naf  aAgricultural engineers2lcsh  afemale  aspa1 aRetamal, Claudia Eugenia Sanhueza  aAproximación al análisis de riesgo basada en las concentraciones de PCBs de las aguas y suelo en la cuenca del río Ñuble ¿es imposiblñe predecir la ingesta de contaminantes orgánicos persistentes en la población?, 2015:btitle page (Claudia Eugenia Sanhueza Retamal; Proyecto de Título, Ingeniero Civil Agrícola, Universidad de Concepción)00597nz  a2200205n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002700115046000700142100001600149370002300165372003100188375001400219377000800233400001600241670013400257no2018110341DLC20180822073033.0