ade her the daughter and successor of Phanes, a creator god)  aThe Oxford classical dictionary, 1996b(Nyx (Ν́υξ), personification of night. In Greek mythology she was a great cosmogonical figure, feared and respected even by Zeus. In Hesiod she is born of Chaos and mother of Aether, Hemera, and lesser powers. In the Orphic Rhapsodies she is daughter of Phanes and succeeds to his power. Nyx was primarily a mythographer's goddess, with little cult)  aTheoi Project website, August 17, 2018b(Nyx; Greek name: Νυξ; Roman name: Nox; goddess of the night, one of the primordial gods (protogenoi) who emerged as the dawn of creation)uhttp://www.theoi.com/Protogenos/Nyx.html00582nz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002300115046002100138100003400159670012400193670010700317no2018110887DLC20180822073134.0180817n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano2018110887  a(OCoLC)oca11506698  aCStbengerdacCSt  s1955-11-102edtf1 aJohnson, Milton,dactive 1955  aJohnson, Milton, Stanford historical photograph collection, 1887-circa 1996 (inclusive), viewed online August 17, 2018.  aStanford historical photos, viewed online August 17, 2018b(Johnson, Milton; photo take Nov. 10, 1955)00406nz  a2200145n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002700115100002100142400002100163670007600184no2018110888DLC20180822073134.0180817n| azannaabn          |a aaa     c  ano2018110888  a(OCoLC)oca11506699  aCSt-HbengerdacCSt-H1 aDel Sar, Alberto1 aSar, Alberto del  aGli orrori della Siberia Argentina, 1927:btitle page (Alberto del Sar)00949nz  a2200217n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002700115046000700142100003600149370005800185372002800243374005000271374002300321375001700344377000800361670036200369no2018110891DLC20180822073134.0180817n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano2018110891  a(OCoLC)oca11506702