cameraman for Universal Pictures, he was a pool photographer assigned to Gen. George S. Patton's command in Europe during World War II. His wartime work included filming the liberation of the Buchenwald concentration camp. Later, sent to the Far East, he documented the Japanese surrender on the deck of the battleship Missouri on Sept. 1, 1945. In his postwar career with the NBC and ABC networks, Mr. Priestley worked on more than 300 news and cultural programs, nine of which won Emmy Awards)  aIMDb, Aug. 16, 2016b(Tom Priestley (III) (1917-1993) director, cinematographer, producer; also worked as a newsreel cameraman. His brother Jack Priestley, and son Tom Priestley Jr. were cameramen too. Born: September 29, 1917 in Fort Lee, New Jersey, USA; Died: January 28, 1993 (age 75) in New York, USA)  aAncestry website, Aug. 16, 2016:bSusan Chipman family tree (Thomas Priestley, Sr., birth: 29 Sep 1917, New Jersey; death: 28 Jan 1993, East Hampton, Suffolk, New York) U.S. Social Security Applications and Claims Index, 1936-2007 (Thomas Anthony Priestley; Birth: 29 Sep 1917 - Fort Lee, New Jersey; Death: 28 Jan 1993)00567nz  a2200193n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002900115042000900144046000900153100004800162377000800210400004000218400003700258670007800295no2018111281DLC20180821073150.0180820n| azannaabn          |a aaa        ano2018111281  a(OCoLC)oca11509712  aSaPrNLbengerdacSaPrNL  asanb  k20181 aFreedman, Claire.tLost penguin.lAfrikaans  aafr1 aFreedman, Claire.tVerlore pikkewyn1 aHindley, Kate.tVerlore pikkewyn  aDie verlore pikkewyn, 2018:btitle page (Claire Freedman en Kate Hindley)00352nz  a2200133n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002500115100002100140670005700161no2018111282DLC20180821073150.0180820n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano2018111282  a(OCoLC)oca11509713  aPPiUbengerdacPPiU1 aĐurisić, Luca  aBabi