0136373008700157373008700244670008400331670076500415no2018111605DLC20180821073336.0180820n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano2018111605  a(OCoLC)oca11510186  aGUbengerdacGU1 aFitzgerald, Judy  aGeorgia. Department of Behavioral Health and Developmental Disabilities2nafs2012  aEmory University. Carter Center. Mental Health ProgramaUniversity of Georgia2naf  aThe Commission on Children's Mental Health, 2017:bcover page (Judy Fitzgerald)  aGeorgia DBHDD website, viewed August 20, 2018:b(Judy Fitzgerald was appointed Commissioner of the Georgia Department of Behavioral Health and Developmental Disabilities by Governor Nathan Deal in 2016. She has been with DBHDD since 2012. Fitzgerald is a social worker with a career-long focus on behavioral health and public service delivery system. Fitzgerald was privileged to begin her career in the Mental Health Program of The Carter Center, working with former First Lady Rosalynn Carter on domestic and international advocacy and policy efforts to promote mental health and reduce the stigma of mental illness. Fitzgerald earned her master's degree in social work from the University of Georgia.)uhttps://dbhdd.georgia.gov/commissioner-judy-fitzgerald00570nz  a2200181n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002300115130004000138643004400178644001100222645001700233646001100250670012700261no2018111606DLC20180821073336.0180820n| azaabaaan          |n ana     c  ano2018111606  a(OCoLC)oca11510187  aInUbengerdacInU 0aNew horizons in East Asian politics  aCheltenham, UKbEdward Elgar Publishing  af5InU  at5DPCC5InU  as5InU  aCheung, Gordon C. K. China in the global political economy, 2018:bseries title page (New horizons in East Asian politics)00741nz  a2200229n  45000010013000000030004000130050017000170080041000340100017000750350023000920400027001151000044001423770008001863800032001943800024002264300030002506430038002806440013003186450