ge of 35 years, as a result of accidental injuries received on January 3, while on duty overseas in the United States Army; he had been engaged for about a year in locating well-sites to develop water-supplies for military establishments in Africa and Asia; he was buried in a British military cemetery in Africa; Major Cady was born in Cortland, New York on August 7, 1907; he graduated from Colgate University, and did postgraduate work at Colgate and Harvard; he was appointed in the Geological Survey, United States Department of the Interior, in 1930, and from 1931 until he began his work in Africa he served continuously in the Ground-Water Division of the Geological Survey; he was a member of the American Geophysical Union, the Society of Economic Geologists, the Geological Society of Washington, and the Sigma Gamma Epsilon and Phi Gamma Delta fraternities)  aancestry.com, August 21, 2018b(Major Richard C. Cady; death date: 15 January 1943; burial place: Carthage, Tunisia)00838nz  a2200229n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002900115046002100144100003900165374001800204378001200222400003300234400003200267400002300299670009800322670006900420670011900489no2018112523DLC20180822073249.0180821n| azannaabn          |b aaa     c  ano2018112523  a(OCoLC)oca11512394  aCSt-HCbengerdacCSt-HC  f1860g19112edtf1 aShapiro, M.q(Moysheh),d1860-1911  aEditors2lcsh  qMoysheh1 aShapiro, Moysheh,d1860-19111 aShapiro, Mosheh,d1860-19111 aשפירא, משה  aNaṭur-ṿisenshafṭlikhe folḳs-bikher, 1910- :btitle page (מ. שפירא = M. Shapiro)  aOCLC, viewed August, 21, 2018b(hdg.: Shapiro, Moshe, 1860-1911)  aBen-Guryon University library catalog, viewed online Augsut 21, 2018b(hdg.: שפירא, משה = Shapiro, Moysheh00578nz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002900115100002300144372002200167374004000189670019100229no2018112524DLC20180823073011.018082