; born 1960)  aVIAF, viewed August 22, 2018.01903nz  a2200217n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002900115100004100144370003400185372004200219374004100261375001700302377000800319670037200327670063400699670035201333no2018113386DLC20180823073125.0180822n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  ano2018113386  a(OCoLC)oca11514637  aMnMHCLbengerdacMnMHCL1 aHardin, Bradc(Motivational speaker)  eNorth Little Rock (Ark.)2naf  aSelf actualization (Psychology)2lcsh  aMotivational speakersaAuthors2lcsh  aMales2lcdgt  aeng  aBrad Hardin. The one full year challenge, 2017:btitle page (Brad Hardin) : page 4 of cover (Brad Hardin was living a "Checklist Christian" life and realized he needed to make some changes ... During his journey, he founded One Full Year, an organization designed to inspire and support people and communities to make long lasting positive changes in their lives...).  aonefullyear.com, via WWW, August 21, 2018bBrad Hardin. About us. Our story. (A message from our founder, Brad Hardin. In 2016, I went on a journey to seek out change in my life.... About 18 months after this journey first started, I wrote and published, "The One Full Year Challenge", to motivate and kick-start people in the right direction towards change and challenging them to grow into the absolute best person possible.... I have been blessed to have spoken to thousands about seeking change in their own life and their communities. My talks are engaging and challenging for all ages...)uhttp://onefullyear.com/our-story/  athv11.com, via WWW, August 21, 2018bBrad Hardin. in article "Arkansas writer urges committment of 'One Full Year' to change," by Erika Ferrando (Brad Hardin of North Little Rock released the book 'One Full Year' in September 2017).uhttps://www.thv11.com/article/news/local/arkansas-writer-urges-commitment-of-one-full-year-to-change/91-50326779300741nz  a2200193n  45000010013000000030004000130