t the same year for Abdullahi Bayero College/Ahmadu Bello University, bachelors in history 1971; in 1972 he joined the North Eastern State Ministry of Education as education officer; assistant lecturer the same year, North East College of Arts and Science (NECAS), Maiduguri; left in 1973 for University of Wisconsin, Madison, master's in education administration; upon return he became assistant registrar II; in 1975 appointed principal assistant registrar at the newly established University of Maiduguri, became its first substantive registrar in 1978; in 1984 appointed Secretary to the Military Government and Head of Service of Gongola State, served for 3 years 6 months; served 3 military governors 1984-1987; in 1988 appointed Federal Commissioner, National Population Commission, Lagos; began political activity in the mid-1970s; joined the Gongola Unity Movement (GUM) in 1978, who metamorphosed into the National Party of Nigeria (NPN) in Gongola State; in 1992 he ran for senator of Adamawa Central District, lost; with the coming of the Fourth Republic, he was a founding member of the People's Democratic Party (PDP) in Adamawa State; later appointed director general, National Boundary Commission; in 2004 he was turbaned the Third Dan Madami Adamawa; also held office as chairman of Adamawa State Civil Service; in 2012 appointed federal commissioner for Public Complaints Commission in charge of Adamawa State Office; he is currently a member of a think tank committee for the economic revival of Adamawa State)01208nz  a2200229n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002300115046002100138100002600159370001700185373004500202374004600247375001700293377000800310400003500318670013200353670049300485no2018113504DLC20180824073011.0180823n| azannaabn          |a aaa     c  ano2018113504  a(OCoLC)oca11514755  aIENbengerdacIEN  f1957-01-012edtf1 aAleiro, Adamu,d1957-  cNigeria2naf  aPeople's Democratic Party (Nigeria